# Normalise line endings so Windows and Linux contributors stop fighting.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf

# No Git LFS rules. The large weights (*.keras, *.safetensors) used to be
# tracked with LFS; they now live on the Hugging Face Hub and are fetched by
# `make fetch-weights` (see src/artifacts.py), so nothing in git needs LFS and
# a clone without `git lfs pull` no longer ends up with pointer stubs.
#
# The small artifacts that stay in git - the LR pipeline (~600 KB), the
# tokenizers (~1.8 MB) and the transformer's config and vocabulary - are
# ordinary blobs on purpose: a plain `git clone` gets a working Logistic
# Regression model, which the CI container job relies on when it asserts a
# real prediction.
